meta {
  name: admin-pan-iocl-card
}

docs {
  # Add a PAN to a torg and create IOCL fuel cards on it, as VAHN_ADMIN (PAN verified by hand in zeus)

  1. `POST /api/pan/without-verification`: add the PAN to the torg as PENDING. No provider call.
  2. (manual) Verify the PAN in zeus. Step 3 needs it VERIFIED.
  3. `POST /api/trucks/attach-to-pan`: point the trucks at the new PAN. IOCL builds the customer from
     the truck's PAN, so without this the card would be made on the torg's old PAN. Attaching also
     queues an automatic fuel card creation for every VERIFIED truck with a driver (IOCL first, then
     BPCL if IOCL fails).
  4. `POST /api/fuel-cards/create-card`: create the IOCL card for one truck. Run it once per truck. If
     the queued creation from step 3 already made the card, it answers statusCode 400 "Active fuel
     card already exists for all attempted providers".

  Run each step on its own (01, then zeus, then 02, then 03 per truck). Pass every input at run time
  so no token or customer data is stored:

      npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/flows/plutus-api/admin-pan-iocl-card/01-add-pan-to-torg.bru --env staging \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclAdminToken=<VAHN_ADMIN token> \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclTorgId=<torg id> \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclPanNumber=<PAN> \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclPhone=<phone> \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclHolderName="<name as on PAN>"

      npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/flows/plutus-api/admin-pan-iocl-card/02-attach-trucks-to-pan.bru --env staging \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclAdminToken=<token> \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclPanNumber=<PAN> \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclTruckIds=101,102

      npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/flows/plutus-api/admin-pan-iocl-card/03-create-iocl-card.bru --env staging \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclAdminToken=<token> \
        --env-var plutusApiAdminPanIoclTruckId=101

  On production add `--env-var baseUrl=https://sapi.vahn.in` (the prod env file has no `baseUrl`).

  Traps:
  - `without-verification` checks neither duplicate PAN numbers nor duplicate phones, and an empty
    `phone` falls back to the caller's (the admin's) phone. Step 1 refuses to send without a phone.
    Check `GET /api/pan/number/{pan}` first if unsure.
  - Do not use `?additional=true` as VAHN_ADMIN: it links the PAN to the admin's own torg. Linking
    through `torgId` in the body keeps the torg's primary PAN as it is.
  - IOCL refuses a mobile it already has ("Mobile Number in permanent address is already exist").
    The IOCL mobile is the PAN's phone.
  - Attach one truck first and wait for its card, then the rest: several queued creations at once can
    race to create the same IOCL customer.
  - IOCL errors come back as a generic 500. Find the cause in Loki with
    `{job="plutus"} |= "for IOCL XtraPower for customer with pan card ID"`.
}
